3.1. Learned advocate for the applicant further submits that the applicant is aged about 85 years and due to his old age, though he was granted bail in the year 2000, he could not remain present with the proceedings of the trial but now, he is ready to file an undertaking before the learned trial court to remain present with the proceedings of the trial and fully cooperate with the proceedings of the trial;
4. On the other hand, learned APP appearing for the respondent - State has vehemently opposed the grant of present application for regular bail and has submitted that looking to the nature of offences affecting the society at large and looking to the facts as well as the allegations made against the applicant accused, no discretion be exercised in favour of the applicant accused.
5. In the facts and circumstances of the case and considering the nature of allegations, this Court is of the opinion that, discretion is required to be exercised to enlarge the applicant accused on regular bail and the following facts have been considered while exercising discretion in favour of the applicant accused:-
(i) the applicant is in jail since 10/08/2023;
NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/16535/2023 ORDER DATED: 18/09/2023 undefined (ii) charge sheet is filed;
(iii) the applicant is earlier granted bail in the year 2000 but as he was not appearing before the trial court, he has been taken into custody by the learned trial court;
(iv) the applicant to file an undertaking before the learned trial court within a period of seven days from the date of this order that he will remain present before the trial court as and when required and fully cooperate with the trial proceedings;
6.

Hence, the present application is allowed and the applicant accused is ordered to be released on regular bail in connection with the FIR being C.R.No.I-295 of 2000 registered with Rajkot "B" Division Police Station, District Rajkot on executing personal bond of Rs.10,000/-
(Rupees Ten thousand only) with one surety of the like amount to the satisfaction of the learned Trial Court and subject to the conditions that he shall;
[a] not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty;
[b] not act in a manner injuries to the interest of the prosecution;
[c] surrender passport, if any, to the lower court within a week;
